        {"id": "839.c", "label": "c", "answer": "\\frac{\\sqrt{6a}}{6}", "derivation": "Numerator=sqrt(a)*(sqrt(a)+sqrt6); denominator=sqrt6*(sqrt(a)+sqrt6). The common sum is positive, leaving sqrt(a)/sqrt6=sqrt(6a)/6.", "domain": "a>=0; 6+sqrt(6a)>0 so a=0 is valid and there is no additional exclusion."},
        {"id": "839.d", "label": "d", "answer": "\\frac{\\sqrt{p}}{2}", "derivation": "Numerator=sqrt(p)*(sqrt(p)-2); denominator=2*(sqrt(p)-2).", "domain": "p>=0 and p!=4; p=0 is valid."},
