        {"id": "843.d", "label": "d", "answer": "6-2\\sqrt{7}", "derivation": "Multiply by 3-sqrt7: 4(3-sqrt7)/(9-7)=2(3-sqrt7). THEN insert root7.", "domain": "3+sqrt7>0.", "table": {"cells": ["IV-root-7"], "coefficients": [-2], "exactConstant": 6, "arithmetic": "6-2*2.646=0.708", "approximation": "0.708", "absoluteErrorBound": "0.0010", "lookupAndArithmeticCompleted": true}},
        {"id": "843.e", "label": "e", "answer": "9+4\\sqrt{5}", "derivation": "Use conjugate 9+4sqrt5; denominator 81-16*5=1. THEN insert root5, rather than divide by a rounded small denominator.", "domain": "9-4sqrt5>0 because 81>80.", "table": {"cells": ["IV-root-5"], "coefficients": [4], "exactConstant": 9, "arithmetic": "9+4*2.236=17.944", "approximation": "17.944", "absoluteErrorBound": "0.0020", "lookupAndArithmeticCompleted": true}},
        {"id": "843.f", "label": "f", "answer": "7+5\\sqrt{2}", "derivation": "Use conjugate 5sqrt2+7; denominator 25*2-49=1. THEN insert root2.", "domain": "5sqrt2-7>0 because 50>49.", "table": {"cells": ["IV-root-2"], "coefficients": [5], "exactConstant": 7, "arithmetic": "7+5*1.414=14.070", "approximation": "14.070", "absoluteErrorBound": "0.0025", "lookupAndArithmeticCompleted": true}}
      ]
    },
    {
      "exercise": "844",
      "grading": "ungraded",
      "tasks": [
        {"id": "844", "label": "proof", "answer": "\\sqrt{\\frac{a+b}{2}}\\ge\\frac{\\sqrt{a}+\\sqrt{b}}{2};\\quad\\text{equality iff }a=b", "derivation": "Both sides are nonnegative for a,b>=0. Left square minus right square=(a+b)/2-(a+b+2sqrt(ab))/4=(sqrt(a)-sqrt(b))^2/4>=0. Hence the inequality follows by monotonicity of squaring on nonnegative numbers. Equality holds exactly when sqrt(a)=sqrt(b), equivalently a=b, including a=b=0.", "domain": "a>=0 and b>=0."}
      ]
    },
    {
      "exercise": "845",
      "grading": "ungraded",
      "tasks": [
        {"id": "845", "label": "comparison", "answer": "\\frac{a+b}{2}\\ge\\sqrt{ab};\\quad\\text{equality iff }a=b", "derivation": "Subtract: (a+b)/2-sqrt(ab)=(sqrt(a)-sqrt(b))^2/2>=0. This gives the comparison without unsupported squaring, and equality exactly when a=b.", "domain": "a>=0 and b>=0."}
      ]
    },
    {
      "exercise": "846",
      "grading": "ungraded",
      "tasks": [
        {
          "id": "846.a",
          "label": "a",
          "answer": "b=\\frac{a(s-m)}{s+m}",
          "derivation": "On the original domain b!=a, multiply by a-b: s(a-b)=m(a+b). Rearrange to (s+m)b=a(s-m). In the ordinary case s+m!=0 divide to obtain the displayed formula; its original denominator is a-b=2am/(s+m), so the candidate is valid only when am!=0. Account for all exceptional cases below.",
          "domain": "a,m,s are real fixed parameters; the original formula requires b!=a.",
          "cases": [
            {"condition": "s+m!=0 and am!=0", "solutionSet": "The single value b=a(s-m)/(s+m)."},
            {"condition": "s+m!=0 and am=0", "solutionSet": "Empty: the only cross-multiplied candidate is b=a, forbidden in the original."},
            {"condition": "s+m=0 and am=0", "solutionSet": "Every real b except b=a. The cross-multiplied equation is the identity 0=0 on the original domain."},
            {"condition": "s+m=0 and am!=0", "solutionSet": "Empty: the cross-multiplied equation requires 0=-2am, impossible."}
          ],
          "substitutionCheck": "For the ordinary valid case, a+b=2as/(s+m) and a-b=2am/(s+m), hence m(a+b)/(a-b)=s."
        },
        {
          "id": "846.b",
          "label": "b",
          "answer": "R=\\frac{d^2-h^2}{2h}",
          "derivation": "The original contains h/(2R), so R!=0 is mandatory before expansion. Expand to d^2=2Rh+h^2. If h!=0, isolate R. If h=0, do not divide by h; use the original equation d^2=0. Preserve the R!=0 exclusion in all cases.",
          "domain": "d,h are real fixed parameters; R is real and R!=0.",
          "cases": [
            {"condition": "h!=0 and d^2!=h^2", "solutionSet": "The single nonzero value R=(d^2-h^2)/(2h)."},
            {"condition": "h!=0 and d^2=h^2", "solutionSet": "Empty: the cross-multiplied candidate R=0 is forbidden."},
            {"condition": "h=0 and d=0", "solutionSet": "Every real nonzero R."},
            {"condition": "h=0 and d!=0", "solutionSet": "Empty."}
          ],
          "optionalPhysicalInterpretation": "If positive lengths d,h,R are separately required, h>0 and d>h give the positive ordinary solution. Positivity is not added to the unrestricted written formula as an unstated source condition."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "exercise": "847",
      "grading": "ungraded",
      "tasks": [
        {"id": "847.a", "label": "a", "answer": "x=0\\text{ or }x=27", "derivation": "Factor x^2-27x=x(x-27); use the zero-product property.", "domain": "x real."},
        {"id": "847.b", "label": "b", "answer": "y=0\\text{ or }y=\\frac{7}{3}", "derivation": "Factor 3y^2-7y=y(3y-7).", "domain": "y real."},
        {"id": "847.c", "label": "c", "answer": "y=\\pm\\frac{1}{4}", "derivation": "16y^2=1 gives y^2=1/16, with both signs.", "domain": "y real."},
        {"id": "847.d", "label": "d", "answer": "\\text{No real solution}", "derivation": "For every real x, 4x^2+1>=1>0. Equivalently x^2=-1/4 is impossible over the reals.", "domain": "x real; complex solutions are outside this lesson's stated real-root scope."},
        {"id": "847.e", "label": "e", "answer": "x=\\pm\\sqrt{5}", "derivation": "x^2=5 gives the positive and negative roots.", "domain": "x real."},
        {"id": "847.f", "label": "f", "answer": "x=\\pm\\sqrt{0.3}=\\pm\\frac{\\sqrt{30}}{10}", "derivation": "Divide by 3: x^2=0.9/3=0.3=3/10, then take both signs.", "domain": "x real."}
      ]
    },
    {
      "exercise": "848",
      "grading": "ungraded",
      "tasks": [
        {"id": "848.1", "label": "y=1.5x+2", "answer": "\\text{line }a", "derivation": "Source/current line a rises through (0,2) and (2,5). Its slope is (5-2)/(2-0)=3/2 and its y-intercept is 2.", "domain": "Linear function for all real x; the figure displays only the source frame.", "graph": {"figure": "fig-56", "coordinates": [[0, 2], [2, 5]], "line": "a", "equation": "y=(3/2)x+2"}},
        {"id": "848.2", "label": "y=-2x+2", "answer": "\\text{line }b", "derivation": "Source/current line b falls through (0,2) and (1,0), giving slope -2 and y-intercept 2.", "domain": "Linear function for all real x; the figure displays only the source frame.", "graph": {"figure": "fig-56", "coordinates": [[0, 2], [1, 0]], "line": "b", "equation": "y=-2x+2"}},
        {"id": "848.3", "label": "y=-x/4-3", "answer": "\\text{line }c", "derivation": "Source/current line c passes through (-12,0) and (0,-3). Its slope is (-3-0)/(0+12)=-1/4 and its y-intercept is -3.", "domain": "Linear function for all real x; the figure displays only the source frame.", "graph": {"figure": "fig-56", "coordinates": [[-12, 0], [0, -3]], "line": "c", "equation": "y=-x/4-3"}}
      ]
    },
